      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nA prompt that already closed its reasoning block must parse the continuation as content on the non-streaming path. For PLaMo3 it was returned as `reasoning` with `content=None`, while streaming returned it as content. This declares the PLaMo3 turn boundary so both agree. Ref #61857.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- Non-streaming returns the continuation as `content` instead of `reasoning` when the prompt already closes the PLaMo3 think block.\r\n- `reasoning_tokens` is 0 for such a turn on both paths. On `main` both streaming and non-streaming counted every generated token as reasoning.\r\n- A new turn after an earlier reasoned answer still parses as reasoning (`EOT` ends the earlier turn).\r\n- No behavior change for other parsers.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nReal checkpoint, tokenizer and chat template: [`pfnet/plamo-3-610m-fin-instruct`](https://huggingface.co/pfnet/plamo-3-610m-fin-instruct) (public PLaMo3 reasoning model). The request goes through `OpenAIServingChat.create_chat_completion` with `--reasoning-parser plamo3`, `continue_final_message=True` and an assistant prefill whose reasoning is closed:\r\n\r\n```\r\nprompt tail : ...<|plamo:val|>think<|plamo:msg|><|plamo:begin_think:plamo|>数字を順番に並べるだけです。<|plamo:end_think:plamo|>1、2、3、4、\r\ncontinuation: 5、6、7、8、9、10です。<|plamo:tag|>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe continuation is the checkpoint's greedy output. No GPU was available, so it was generated with the HF reference implementation on CPU and replayed into the serving layer; the rendered prompt token ids are identical to HF's.\r\n\r\nBefore (`main` at 2365177ddd):\r\n```\r\nnon-stream  reasoning='5、6、7、8、9、10です。'  content=None  reasoning_tokens=13\r\nstream      reasoning=''  content='5、6、7、8、9、10です。'  reasoning_tokens=13\r\n```\r\nAfter (this PR):\r\n```\r\nnon-stream  reasoning=None  content='5、6、7、8、9、10です。'  reasoning_tokens=0\r\nstream      reasoning=''  content='5、6、7、8、9、10です。'  reasoning_tokens=0\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/parser/engine/test_plamo3.py -q\r\n122 passed\r\n```\r\nThe new test fails on the base for both the direct and registered parser paths.\r\n\r\nNot covered: a prefill without a think block (`{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"1、2、3、4、\"}`). The model continues it as answer text, and it is still returned as reasoning, as on `main`. The prompt has no closed think block in that case, so this change does not apply.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\nRoot cause: `ParserEngine.set_prompt_token_ids` applies the prompt-closed state only when the config declares `turn_boundary_tokens` (ref #61857), and PLaMo3 declared none. \r\nFix: add `turn_boundary_tokens=frozenset({EOT})`, where `EOT` (`<|plamo:tag|>`, id 16) is the PLaMo3 turn terminator and already stops `Plamo3Parser.is_reasoning_end`.\r\n\r\nOut of scope: the direct-engine streaming path does not apply `_prompt_closes_reasoning`; production uses the registered delegating parser.\r\n\r\nDuplicate check: no PLaMo3 issue or PR covers this; #61857 is the parent and is merged.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>",
